 HOW TO MAKE YOUR PHONE THE MASTER (No computer needed)     
╚═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

📦 WHAT YOU NEED:
────────────────
• Arduino Uno/Nano + HC-05 Bluetooth module
• Your phone (Android or iPhone)
• USB cable (just for first-time code upload)

🔌 STEP 1: WIRE IT
────────────────
HC-05    →    Arduino
TX       →    RX (pin 0)
RX       →    TX (pin 1)
VCC      →    5V
GND      →    GND

⚠️ Unplug RX/TX when uploading code. Plug back after.

📲 STEP 2: UPLOAD CODE TO ARDUINO
─────────────────────────────────
1. Open Arduino IDE on a computer (just once)
2. Paste the code from this chat
3. Disconnect RX/TX wires
4. Click Upload
5. Reconnect RX/TX wires

🎯 STEP 3: PAIR YOUR PHONE
─────────────────────────
1. Turn on Bluetooth
2. Scan for devices
3. Find "HC-05"
4. PIN: 1234 or 0000

📱 STEP 4: DOWNLOAD APP
───────────────────────
Search "Serial Bluetooth Terminal" in your app store.
Download it. It's free.

🔗 STEP 5: CONNECT
─────────────────
1. Open the app
2. Tap connect (📎 or 🔌 icon)
3. Select "HC-05"

✅ STEP 6: TEST IT
─────────────────
Type: PING
Send it.

You should see: PONG

If you see garbage text, change baud rate to 9600 in app settings.

⛏️ STEP 7: GET A JOB
────────────────────
You need three things from DUCO server:
• last_hash (40 chars)
• target_hash (40 chars)  
• difficulty (number)

Get these from DUCO web dashboard or by running a script on a PC.

📤 STEP 8: SEND JOB TO ARDUINO
─────────────────────────────
Type this format:

JOB,last_hash,target_hash,difficulty

Example:
JOB,ffe0e47b591d542be3e9d8aeaeedebcbaa602095,0000a3f2b1c4e5d6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8,45

Hit send. Arduino replies: JOB_READY

⏳ STEP 9: WAIT
──────────────
Arduino mines for 10-60 seconds.
You'll see: FOUND,12345

🎉 STEP 10: SUBMIT
─────────────────
Go to DUCO website → Manual share submission.
Enter your username and the nonce (12345).
If it says GOOD, you just mined!

🔄 STEP 11: REPEAT
─────────────────
Get another job. Send it. Wait. Submit.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

⚠️ QUICK FIXES

No PONG?              → Check wiring, reconnect Bluetooth
Garbage text?         → Set baud rate to 9600
Upload fails?         → Disconnect RX/TX first
Job not found?        → Wrong format, check commas
No response?          → Reset Arduino (press reset button)

